--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI BackupRestorePage at web parity: a pure @Observable state
holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable BackupRestoreDataSource
seam whose value types mirror the web BackupConfig / BackupRun / RestorePreview 1:1
(production binds the shared core's /backup/* endpoints through the seam). The page
reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title/subtitle + the Quick Backup / New Config
header actions), the four web MetricCard stat tiles, and BOTH web GlassPanels:

  Stat tiles    — Total Configs / Total Backups / Last Backup / Total Size (TSStatCard),
                  with a four-up TSStatSkeleton loading row.
  GlassPanel5   — Backup Configurations: an adaptive table (columnar Grid on macOS/iPad,
                  per-row cards on iPhone) with the web columns (name + Disabled badge,
                  type, provider, frequency, schedule, options) and per-row Trigger / Edit
                  / Delete actions.
  GlassPanel6   — Backup History: a horizontally-scrollable adaptive table (time, run type,
                  status, provider, file, size, records, duration) with Download / Verify /
                  Preview actions on completed runs, followed by the Recent Errors list.

The create/edit Modal, the delete ConfirmDialog, and the restore-preview Modal are
presented as HIG-native sheets sharing a BackupSheetScaffold. The editor reproduces the
web form (name, enabled, type, provider, frequency, retention, the dynamic per-provider
credential fields, compress/encrypt) with the web Save guard; the delete sheet confirms a
permanent removal; the preview sheet shows the checksum status, metadata, and restorable
tables (with a loading state). The web toast results are surfaced as a dismissible
TSAlertBanner (BackupOutcome). SI is honored: bytes/ms/ISO are stored raw and formatted only
at the display boundary by BackupRestoreFormat (ports of the web formatBytes / fmtInt /
formatDurationMsCompact / formatRelative).

